WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:28.208
Your grandmother made my graduation dress.

2
00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:31.166
No wonder it looked horrible
in the photos.

3
00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:34.208
-And did you have a boyfriend then?
-Yes.

4
00:00:34.291 --> 00:00:36.666
Was he handsome?
I haven't seen any pictures.

5
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.041
Luckily. there were no cell phones
or social media back in the day.

6
00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:45.041
And yes. he was handsome.
but never as handsome as your dad.

7
00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:47.125
Nobody is more handsome than my dad.

8
00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:48.625
Nobody.

9
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:54.250
Mom. can I ask you
for a special graduation gift?

10
00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:59.958
After my party. I want to go
to an after-party with my friends.

11
00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:01.291
Victoria is coming!

12
00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:05.416
There are tables and chairs outside.

13
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.208
We hired several waiters.

14
00:01:07.291 --> 00:01:10.250
There's a stage
for you to sing with your dad.

15
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:17.041
So why don't you invite everyone
and have the after-party here?

16
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:19.625
There are no parents at the after-party.

17
00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:22.333
I promise I won't drink.
even if they try to force me.

18
00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:23.791
Let's ask your dad.

19
00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:27.041
In the name of our president.
I approve of this.

20
00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:31.916
-Your dad will drive you and pick you up.
-Of course.

21
00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:36.458
But first. miss.

22
00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:38.375
let's do a mic check.

23
00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:39.708
-Yes.
-Okay?

24
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:41.500
Whose eyes are those?

25
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.291
Dad. I'm almost 18.

26
00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:45.791
Whose eyes are those?

27
00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:47.125
Yours.

28
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:50.250
My makeup.

29
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.625
I love you.

30
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:54.041
We're so proud of you. sweetheart.

31
00:01:54.125 --> 00:01:57.791
And that's why we have a surprise for you.
it's your graduation gift.

32
00:01:57.875 --> 00:02:00.583
and there's a whole committee
waiting for you. so let's go.

33
00:02:00.666 --> 00:02:02.541
Okay. I'm coming. Just give me a second.

34
00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:04.708
-Yes. Let's go.
-Don't take too long.

35
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:29.125
-She's coming!
-Did she dress up?

36
00:02:29.208 --> 00:02:30.375
Enough.

37
00:02:32.166 --> 00:02:33.000
Ready?

38
00:02:33.916 --> 00:02:36.208
What could this be?

39
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:38.125
Nana.

40
00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:41.250
-No way!
-Yeah!

41
00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:43.958
-No! Is it what I'm thinking?
-Yes!

42
00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:50.750
Bravo!

43
00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:52.833
You're going to let me drive it?

44
00:02:52.916 --> 00:02:55.125
I'm a bit strict for your own good.

45
00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.583
That's why I took you to get your license.

46
00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:01.833
Congratulations again. Do you like it?

47
00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:04.333
Sweetheart. you deserve everything.

48
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:05.583
You earned it.

49
00:03:05.666 --> 00:03:08.333
You've been working so hard
since your illness started.

50
00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:10.125
You're the coolest of the three of us.

51
00:03:10.208 --> 00:03:13.250
You're going to ruin your makeup
if you cry. you know?

52
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.458
Come on. let's hug.

53
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:17.791
Sotomayor hug!

54
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:19.541
Congratulations!

55
00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:20.500
Look who's here.

56
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:22.125
Victoria!

57
00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:24.791
Check out my graduation gift!

58
00:03:24.875 --> 00:03:26.833
-Yolanda. how are you?
-Fine. and you?

59
00:03:26.916 --> 00:03:27.875
-Hi. Maria.
-Hi.

60
00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:29.583
-Nice to see you. Yolanda.
-Emilio.

61
00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:32.625
-Thanks for having us.
-It's our pleasure. Thanks for coming.

62
00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:34.791
Your mom's letting you go
to the after-party?

63
00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:36.000
Yes!

64
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:39.666
After-party? Victoria hasn't asked us
for permission to go to any after-party.

65
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.291
Did she tell you anything?

66
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:43.958
Juana told me
that a lot of cute boys are coming.

67
00:03:44.041 --> 00:03:44.875
No way!

68
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.458
Ever since she turned 18.
she thinks she's her own boss.

69
00:03:48.541 --> 00:03:51.875
Yeah. you have no idea
what you're in for when Julieta turns 18.

70
00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:54.333
-Let's not even talk about it. Come in.
-We're not there yet.

71
00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:56.458
I'm losing my virginity tonight!

72
00:03:56.541 --> 00:03:57.916
Oh. yeah!

73
00:03:59.041 --> 00:04:00.958
Grandpa. you scared me.

74
00:04:01.041 --> 00:04:04.250
-Congratulations!
-Grandpa!

75
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:08.125
Love you. honey!

76
00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:24.708
There you go!

77
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.125
Somewhere in a large country

78
00:04:37.916 --> 00:04:39.666
Ricardo and Julieta are one and the same.

79
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.291
People forgot to build

80
00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:46.000
And Maca just won't quit.
She's danced with all the guests.

81
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:49.666
A place where the sun won't burn you

82
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.916
My grandkids and my son
are professional artists.

83
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.208
…don't have to die

84
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:13.625
Julieta!

85
00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:14.666
What happened?

86
00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:17.875
Julieta. sweetheart!

87
00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:24.958
No. There's no time for an ambulance.
Let's go.

88
00:05:25.041 --> 00:05:26.250
Excuse me!

89
00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:29.375
There's no time for an ambulance.
Let's go.

90
00:05:29.458 --> 00:05:30.833
-Please. pick her up.
-Okay.

91
00:05:30.916 --> 00:05:32.500
-Careful.
-Excuse me.

92
00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:34.291
Careful.

93
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.666
Careful. Please. be careful.

94
00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:40.458
Let's go.

95
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:50.958
MY DAUGHTER'S FATHER
CREATED BY ROBERTO STOPELLO

96
00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:53.833
CENTRAL STANDARD TIME

97
00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:11.083
I'LL TEXT YOU AS SOON
AS WE KNOW SOMETHING. LOVE YOU.

98
00:06:19.416 --> 00:06:20.250
Maca.

99
00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:24.375
How is she?

100
00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:26.708
-What's with the face?
-You had blood drawn?

101
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:31.791
Yes. She had a severe crisis.
but she's responding to treatment now.

102
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:32.875
How serious is it?

103
00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:37.791
The moment we were dreading is here.
Julieta urgently needs a transplant…

104
00:06:38.291 --> 00:06:39.458
-But--
-But what?

105
00:06:39.541 --> 00:06:42.291
Your kidney is a match for hers. right?

106
00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:45.041
Julieta's blood protein levels
are significantly abnormal.

107
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:47.166
That's why I ordered a special test.

108
00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.958
And we found a genetic disorder.

109
00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:52.958
What does this have to do
with Julieta's transplant?

110
00:06:53.041 --> 00:06:54.750
It's called Alport syndrome.

111
00:06:54.833 --> 00:06:56.708
It's asymptomatic in most women.

112
00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:59.541
and since they both have it.
the transplant wouldn't work.

113
00:06:59.625 --> 00:07:00.708
Is it hereditary?

114
00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:03.791
Yes. Your mom probably inherited it
from her parents or grandparents.

115
00:07:03.875 --> 00:07:05.791
and Julieta from Maca or her grandparents.

116
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:07.750
It could also come from my family. right?

117
00:07:07.833 --> 00:07:09.958
It's impossible to know
without a DNA test.

118
00:07:10.041 --> 00:07:14.083
Well. test me to see if I'm a match.
if I have the syndrome. DNA. everything.

119
00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:15.416
-I'm doing it too.
-Me too.

120
00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.000
Thank you. Thank you.

121
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:29.125
The embarrassment of the year.

122
00:07:29.666 --> 00:07:31.833
I hope no one posts it on Instagram.

123
00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:39.875
I want to go home.
I want to drive my new car.

124
00:07:40.583 --> 00:07:42.500
Of course. sweetheart.

125
00:07:43.708 --> 00:07:45.250
Your kidneys are acting up.

126
00:07:45.916 --> 00:07:48.208
You're sugarcoating bad news. right?

127
00:07:52.791 --> 00:07:53.708
Am I going to die?

128
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:55.291
-No.
-Of course not. sweetheart.

129
00:07:55.916 --> 00:07:59.750
You just need some backup.
A kidney transplant. as soon as possible.

130
00:08:01.666 --> 00:08:04.166
So. are you going to have
just one kidney now?

131
00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.166
I'd give you both if I could.

132
00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.875
But we discovered something.

133
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:17.000
Mom can't donate it anymore. but your
brothers and I are going to get tested.

134
00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.708
Everything will be fine. sweetheart. Okay?

135
00:08:39.666 --> 00:08:41.666
Stop arguing with your mom. Julieta.

136
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.041
Can't you see she's always scolding me?

137
00:08:44.125 --> 00:08:46.958
My dear! It's so good to see you back!

138
00:08:47.041 --> 00:08:48.291
I'll take this.

139
00:08:48.375 --> 00:08:49.666
Thank you.

140
00:08:51.083 --> 00:08:53.541
From now on.
you can't miss a single dialysis.

141
00:08:53.625 --> 00:08:54.666
-No excuses.
-Stop it.

142
00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.416
-You're not a nephrologist.
-Hey. Julieta!

143
00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.833
This is serious.

144
00:08:58.916 --> 00:09:01.750
We have to be stricter
with what we eat in this house. please.

145
00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:02.791
Stricter?

146
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:04.583
I always cook according to her diet--

147
00:09:04.666 --> 00:09:05.958
Hey!

148
00:09:07.041 --> 00:09:10.458
You've been secretly eating junk food.
haven't you? Did you drink at the party?

149
00:09:12.041 --> 00:09:14.791
Could you two calm down. please? Maca!

150
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:27.291
How many times do I have to tell you
that this is poison for your kidneys?

151
00:09:27.375 --> 00:09:30.333
Swear to me that you didn't drink
a single drop of alcohol.

152
00:09:30.416 --> 00:09:31.583
Did you drink?

153
00:09:34.375 --> 00:09:36.125
It was just one tequila shot.

154
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.541
I'm done! I can't lift a finger without
your consent. I do everything wrong!

155
00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:42.458
Sweetheart. you know
this is for your own good.

156
00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:44.166
I'll never be normal again.

157
00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.750
Don't say that.
One of us will be a match. I promise.

158
00:09:48.833 --> 00:09:50.750
Mom promised too. and look at this.

159
00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:53.750
I inherited this fucking syndrome
from you. This is all your fault.

160
00:09:53.833 --> 00:09:56.708
I don't want to live like a prisoner.
following orders all the time.

161
00:09:56.791 --> 00:09:58.500
I'm tired. I can't take it anymore!

162
00:09:58.583 --> 00:10:00.041
Julieta…

163
00:10:00.125 --> 00:10:01.500
Let her go.

164
00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.416
She's right. though.

165
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.541
She inherited the worst of me.

166
00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:40.708
Bernardo can't keep bringing
junk food into this house. Nana.

167
00:10:40.791 --> 00:10:43.000
It's too tempting for Julieta.

168
00:10:44.833 --> 00:10:47.458
There's not a single drop of alcohol
in this house. right?

169
00:10:47.541 --> 00:10:50.166
No. ma'am.
I've even checked under the mattresses.

170
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.958
Like a prison!

171
00:11:12.125 --> 00:11:12.958
Ma'am…

172
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.416
Finally. Julieta is out of the hospital.

173
00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.458
I'm glad.

174
00:11:38.541 --> 00:11:40.833
But Maca couldn't donate her kidney.

175
00:11:40.916 --> 00:11:46.333
Her dad and brothers had to get tested.
but if they're not a match. we should go.

176
00:11:47.666 --> 00:11:51.625
Listen. Victoria. I'm really sorry
about what's happening to Julieta.

177
00:11:51.708 --> 00:11:54.250
but a kidney transplant
is a serious thing.

178
00:11:54.333 --> 00:11:58.583
-And dangerous. too.
-And you get a huge scar. like this.

179
00:11:58.666 --> 00:11:59.750
No way.

180
00:11:59.833 --> 00:12:03.666
What about solidarity? Why are we friends
with the Sotomayors. then?

181
00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.583
It's one thing to be friends.

182
00:12:05.666 --> 00:12:08.791
but it's another thing to have one
of my daughters give up a kidney.

183
00:12:08.875 --> 00:12:10.916
That's not happening!

184
00:12:34.291 --> 00:12:36.000
You finally made it.

185
00:12:36.625 --> 00:12:40.000
As usual. I was arguing with my mom.

186
00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:41.958
How do you feel?

187
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.750
Like I need an urgent kidney transplant.

188
00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:48.333
Other than that. I'm great.

189
00:12:48.416 --> 00:12:49.708
Jerk.

190
00:12:50.541 --> 00:12:53.375
I got FOMO from the after-party pics.
I can't believe I missed it.

191
00:12:53.458 --> 00:12:55.166
I heard Camila left with two guys.

192
00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.083
-No way! Two guys?
-Two guys.

193
00:12:57.166 --> 00:13:00.791
I doubt I'm going to get anyone
to eat me before the worms do.

194
00:13:01.625 --> 00:13:05.083
Speaking of guys. I made
some nice videos with you and your dad.

195
00:13:05.166 --> 00:13:07.291
I can send them over so you can post them.

196
00:13:07.875 --> 00:13:10.416
What for?
My last post only got seven likes.

197
00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.333
We're not influencers. girl. Get over it.

198
00:13:13.416 --> 00:13:18.041
Unless you post pics in your underwear
with your tits up here.

199
00:13:18.125 --> 00:13:19.583
forget about the likes.

200
00:13:20.291 --> 00:13:24.125
That doesn't sound so bad. you know?
But my mom would freak out.

201
00:13:24.208 --> 00:13:27.833
She found my candy. I had to confess
I had one tequila shot at the party.

202
00:13:27.916 --> 00:13:30.833
-You didn't tell her it was me?
-Of course not. She'd kill you.

203
00:13:31.416 --> 00:13:33.750
She even told me
I can't drive the car they gave me.

204
00:13:33.833 --> 00:13:37.125
With good reason. girl.
Imagine if you faint while driving.

205
00:13:37.208 --> 00:13:39.750
That'd be an early grave for you.

206
00:13:40.541 --> 00:13:42.583
Sorry. sorry. sorry.

207
00:13:43.083 --> 00:13:45.416
It's not like I have
a long life ahead of me.

208
00:13:47.458 --> 00:13:48.625
You're too much.

209
00:13:49.125 --> 00:13:50.833
We have to do our best to stay calm.

210
00:13:52.416 --> 00:13:54.958
Let's see what happens
with tomorrow's results.

211
00:13:55.041 --> 00:13:57.041
If nobody's a match.
what are we going to do?

212
00:13:59.916 --> 00:14:01.958
I checked the national donor center.

213
00:14:02.041 --> 00:14:04.291
and there are 4.000 patients
ahead of Julieta.

214
00:14:04.375 --> 00:14:08.958
So. that's not an option.
What about the hospital's private list?

215
00:14:09.041 --> 00:14:12.958
We're doing better. but it'll take
at least six months to get anything.

216
00:14:16.166 --> 00:14:19.666
Jiménez was very clear. Ricardo.
We're running out of time.

217
00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:23.916
We have to be prepared
and raise as much money as possible.

218
00:14:27.916 --> 00:14:29.041
Listen…

219
00:14:30.708 --> 00:14:36.583
You sometimes operate on patients who are
seriously ill. even terminally ill. right?

220
00:14:38.375 --> 00:14:44.208
And if one of those patients
had a kidney that was a match for Julieta.

221
00:14:44.875 --> 00:14:46.208
maybe we could…

222
00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:50.083
I don't know.
jump the hospital's waiting list and…

223
00:14:50.166 --> 00:14:51.208
No…

224
00:14:51.291 --> 00:14:53.208
-What?
-What are you talking about?

225
00:14:53.291 --> 00:14:55.208
Do you understand what you're saying?

226
00:15:00.458 --> 00:15:03.208
Then I won't tell you
what I was thinking about in the shower.

227
00:15:03.291 --> 00:15:05.750
What were you thinking about
in the shower?

228
00:15:07.791 --> 00:15:08.916
Organ trafficking.

229
00:15:09.875 --> 00:15:11.541
How could you think of that?

230
00:15:11.625 --> 00:15:16.333
Not only is it illegal. it's unethical.
We could go to jail.

231
00:15:16.416 --> 00:15:19.375
If that's what I have to do
to save my daughter's life.

232
00:15:19.458 --> 00:15:20.583
I don't care about jail.

233
00:15:20.666 --> 00:15:23.291
Sure! You'll be able
to help her a lot more from jail.

234
00:15:23.375 --> 00:15:28.291
Ricardo! Are you implying that
I don't care about my daughter's life?

235
00:15:33.625 --> 00:15:37.625
I'm sorry. Forgive me. please. I'm upset.

236
00:15:38.791 --> 00:15:40.625
I shouldn't have yelled. I'm sorry.

237
00:15:42.875 --> 00:15:44.750
I just want to remind you…

238
00:15:46.333 --> 00:15:50.083
that you taught me. and it's one
of the things I'm most grateful for.

239
00:15:50.666 --> 00:15:52.958
that nothing is
more important than family.

240
00:16:05.583 --> 00:16:07.041
This can't be right.

241
00:16:08.125 --> 00:16:09.583
I'm not a match either?

242
00:16:09.666 --> 00:16:13.375
Neither are the kids or Nana. Nobody.
We're not a match.

243
00:16:14.458 --> 00:16:16.625
What about that syndrome?

244
00:16:16.708 --> 00:16:17.625
Lorena called.

245
00:16:17.708 --> 00:16:21.666
She said the DNA results will be ready
by the end of the day. at the latest.

246
00:16:22.625 --> 00:16:24.041
Does Julieta know about this?

247
00:16:24.125 --> 00:16:27.041
Gustavo and Bernardo
told me they wanted to tell her.

248
00:16:27.125 --> 00:16:28.458
Good idea.

249
00:16:29.583 --> 00:16:33.666
By the way. Emilio called me.
offering his help with anything we need.

250
00:16:34.458 --> 00:16:36.250
Well. we need a kidney.

251
00:16:36.333 --> 00:16:39.291
Yeah. I was thinking
about asking my parents.

252
00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:41.250
They might still be donors. right?

253
00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:42.750
If they're healthy. yeah.

254
00:16:42.833 --> 00:16:45.000
The kids asked all their friends.

255
00:16:45.083 --> 00:16:47.375
None of them volunteered. so…

256
00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.041
This sucks. Ricardo.

257
00:16:50.125 --> 00:16:55.291
They say you find out who your real
friends are when the going gets rough.

258
00:16:55.375 --> 00:16:58.041
A donor has to show up
at some point. damn it.

259
00:16:59.458 --> 00:17:00.291
Hello?

260
00:17:00.375 --> 00:17:03.791
Hi. Maca. It's me.
I need to talk to you in private.

261
00:17:03.875 --> 00:17:05.916
Come right away. please.

262
00:17:06.416 --> 00:17:08.166
-Okay.
-And don't bring Ricardo.

263
00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.625
Yes. got it.

264
00:17:11.041 --> 00:17:12.625
Okay. I'm on my way.

265
00:17:13.125 --> 00:17:14.041
Bye.

266
00:17:14.541 --> 00:17:18.416
Jiménez. We have a surgery in two hours.
I need to get going now.

267
00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.500
Okay.

268
00:17:26.625 --> 00:17:28.625
Are you gonna tell me where we're going?

269
00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.125
Time to try it out.

270
00:17:38.125 --> 00:17:39.625
Go. Be careful.

271
00:17:55.625 --> 00:17:57.125
The results are in.

272
00:18:02.125 --> 00:18:03.666
Nobody is a match.

273
00:18:06.375 --> 00:18:08.125
If I die. will you remember me forever?

274
00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:10.875
You're not going to die.
Get that crap out of your head.

275
00:18:10.958 --> 00:18:13.250
I heard my parents talking.

276
00:18:13.333 --> 00:18:15.000
They're not gonna give up.

277
00:18:15.083 --> 00:18:18.541
But you'll be left without an inheritance
if they keep spending on me.

278
00:18:18.625 --> 00:18:21.583
As soon as you get better. open
an OnlyFans account to pay them off.

279
00:18:22.666 --> 00:18:24.250
All right. let's toast.

280
00:18:24.333 --> 00:18:25.541
To your health.

281
00:18:25.625 --> 00:18:28.333
And as Dad says. two cheers.
because it's alcohol-free.

282
00:18:28.416 --> 00:18:29.583
-Cheers. cheers.
-Cheers.

283
00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.541
Thank you for being the best.

284
00:18:39.041 --> 00:18:43.666
For the car surprise.
for lifting my spirits.

285
00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:45.958
and for being such good brothers.

286
00:18:48.375 --> 00:18:50.500
Now let's toast to something I don't have.

287
00:18:51.083 --> 00:18:52.708
-To what?
-To my health.

288
00:18:53.291 --> 00:18:54.500
Knock it off. Julieta.

289
00:18:55.375 --> 00:18:56.500
Cheers.

290
00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:01.208
Julieta is very depressed.
She could die. We have to help her.

291
00:19:01.291 --> 00:19:03.375
What can we do for her. sweetie?

292
00:19:03.458 --> 00:19:06.375
I already told her that giving up
her kidney is not a joke.

293
00:19:07.041 --> 00:19:10.708
I'm of legal age. so I can do it.
And. as a matter of fact. I want to help--

294
00:19:10.791 --> 00:19:13.916
At your age. you won't give away
your kidney to a high school classmate.

295
00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:17.041
Besides. you don't know
if you'll still be friends in ten years.

296
00:19:17.125 --> 00:19:20.166
Truth is. you don't even know
if you'll still be close to Julieta.

297
00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:21.958
To give you some peace of mind.

298
00:19:22.041 --> 00:19:24.500
I talked to Ricardo
and told him they can count on us.

299
00:19:24.583 --> 00:19:26.916
That means getting tested
to see if we're a match.

300
00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.791
Sweetie. this is the most important
project of my career!

301
00:19:29.875 --> 00:19:32.083
It's a stadium
for 50.000 people in South Africa.

302
00:19:32.166 --> 00:19:36.000
So a fucking stadium
is more important than Julieta's life?

303
00:19:36.083 --> 00:19:39.333
-I didn't say that. I just--
-Thanks. Dad! That's great! Perfect.

304
00:19:39.416 --> 00:19:40.875
Victoria. come here. Don't be rude.

305
00:19:40.958 --> 00:19:43.416
-You two are impossible.
-It's fine. She'll get over it.

306
00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.833
Young people think everything is forever.
Love. friendships. blood pacts…

307
00:19:47.916 --> 00:19:49.625
The only cure for it is to grow up.

308
00:19:49.708 --> 00:19:52.375
Victoria is light years away from that.

309
00:19:56.125 --> 00:19:57.291
What is it?

310
00:19:58.291 --> 00:20:01.041
-Hey.
-Why did you tell me not to bring Ricardo?

311
00:20:01.625 --> 00:20:03.458
Your daughter has a new opportunity.

312
00:20:03.541 --> 00:20:05.416
And my husband can't know about it?

313
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.333
The DNA results are in.

314
00:20:07.416 --> 00:20:10.791
Neither your children
nor your husband have Alport syndrome.

315
00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.166
That's good news!

316
00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.916
Yes. but there's something else.

317
00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:16.750
Something serious.

318
00:20:16.833 --> 00:20:20.541
Even though we've known each other
for so long and we trust each other.

319
00:20:20.625 --> 00:20:22.375
you still never told me.

320
00:20:47.791 --> 00:20:48.916
Maca?

321
00:20:50.416 --> 00:20:52.083
Maca. girl!

322
00:21:09.791 --> 00:21:11.625
Maca. what's wrong?

323
00:21:15.125 --> 00:21:16.625
I just found out…

324
00:21:18.541 --> 00:21:21.041
that Julieta is not my husband's daughter.

325
00:21:23.083 --> 00:21:27.291
We're in the house of the mom with
the record for the world's biggest bump!

326
00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:28.500
It was huge!

327
00:21:28.583 --> 00:21:30.458
And the most beautiful bump!

328
00:21:31.166 --> 00:21:32.791
-How big is your bump?
-That's you!

329
00:21:33.375 --> 00:21:35.208
-Don't measure it!
-What do you think?

330
00:21:35.291 --> 00:21:36.708
Three meters!

331
00:21:36.791 --> 00:21:39.041
Bernardo! He's so cute!

332
00:21:39.125 --> 00:21:40.458
-Pee.
-No!

333
00:21:40.541 --> 00:21:41.416
I love it.

334
00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.791
Now? Boys. let's go.

335
00:21:43.875 --> 00:21:48.000
-Calm down. Let's breathe.
-I'll get the bag. Where is it?

336
00:21:48.083 --> 00:21:49.708
-Where's the bag? The bag!
-Boys?

337
00:21:49.791 --> 00:21:50.916
Don't forget the bag.

338
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.666
-Don't leave my side.
-The keys?

339
00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:55.208
This video made my day. Dad.

340
00:21:56.416 --> 00:21:59.041
And I have a private collection
you've never seen before.

341
00:21:59.125 --> 00:22:00.666
I want to see them all.

342
00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:01.750
Sure.

343
00:22:01.833 --> 00:22:03.708
That way I forget that I'm sick.

344
00:22:03.791 --> 00:22:06.333
and I'm reminded I have
the best parents in the world.

345
00:22:06.416 --> 00:22:10.625
And we have the bravest
and most badass daughter in the world.

346
00:22:11.875 --> 00:22:12.875
Hey. love.

347
00:22:14.208 --> 00:22:15.958
-Hi. sweetie.
-Hi.

348
00:22:16.041 --> 00:22:18.250
The surgery is already finished?

349
00:22:18.333 --> 00:22:19.750
It got canceled.

350
00:22:19.833 --> 00:22:21.208
That's great.

351
00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:24.875
How are you feeling. sweetie?

352
00:22:24.958 --> 00:22:28.875
Well. I found out neither my dad.
nor my nanny. nor my siblings are a match.

353
00:22:28.958 --> 00:22:31.916
But the DNA results came in.

354
00:22:32.708 --> 00:22:34.583
Nobody has the syndrome.

355
00:22:34.666 --> 00:22:35.875
Just you and me.

356
00:22:36.833 --> 00:22:40.333
I'm your clone. They say the last child
always gets the leftovers.

357
00:22:40.416 --> 00:22:41.708
Julieta…

358
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.958
-Victoria's here. See you tonight.
-Take care. sweetheart.

359
00:22:56.291 --> 00:22:57.833
Hey. stop.

360
00:22:58.916 --> 00:23:00.583
Don't make that face. love.

361
00:23:01.791 --> 00:23:03.041
Look at me.

362
00:23:03.125 --> 00:23:05.833
I'm her dad.
and I can't give her my kidney either.

363
00:23:09.083 --> 00:23:10.833
I have to tell you something.

364
00:23:12.916 --> 00:23:14.791
Yeah. sure. What is it?

365
00:23:19.833 --> 00:23:21.375
What is it. Maca?

366
00:23:23.458 --> 00:23:25.083
It's just that…

367
00:23:30.666 --> 00:23:32.875
It's nothing. That video got to me.

368
00:23:35.958 --> 00:23:39.041
Sometimes the past comes back
and hits you really hard.

369
00:23:43.583 --> 00:23:47.000
Julieta is our miracle child.

370
00:23:49.666 --> 00:23:51.916
She saved our marriage. honey.

371
00:24:08.125 --> 00:24:09.541
No. Bernardo! Stop!

372
00:24:09.625 --> 00:24:13.541
-Don't do that. Give me the spoon.
-Mom. I want milk.

373
00:24:13.625 --> 00:24:16.791
No. sweetie. Do you want milk?
Yes. I'll give you some milk. Wait.

374
00:24:19.041 --> 00:24:23.208
Hey. guys! Dad's here!

375
00:24:26.291 --> 00:24:27.750
What's up. Maca?

376
00:24:27.833 --> 00:24:33.000
I made a thousand pesos.
and I brought the diapers you…

377
00:24:35.250 --> 00:24:37.416
Shit. I left them on the bus. sorry.

378
00:24:37.500 --> 00:24:39.625
Don't swear in front of the children!

379
00:24:41.208 --> 00:24:42.333
We need to talk.

380
00:24:42.416 --> 00:24:45.500
My mom died six months ago.

381
00:24:45.583 --> 00:24:48.333
She was the only one
who helped me with the kids.

382
00:24:48.416 --> 00:24:52.291
I take two-minute showers. Ricardo.
with the kids in the bathroom. of course.

383
00:24:52.375 --> 00:24:56.083
I couldn't enroll this semester
because we can't even afford daycare.

384
00:24:56.166 --> 00:24:59.500
We had to move back
to the place my mom used to live in.

385
00:24:59.583 --> 00:25:01.750
My career went down the drain!

386
00:25:01.833 --> 00:25:06.791
My life went down the drain
because my husband lives from bar to bar.

387
00:25:06.875 --> 00:25:09.375
from serenade to serenade.
and from drink to drink!

388
00:25:09.458 --> 00:25:12.333
-You're drunk!
-Maca. wait. I promise you I--

389
00:25:12.416 --> 00:25:14.291
No! I've fucking had it
with your promises!

390
00:25:14.375 --> 00:25:15.458
I've fucking had it!

391
00:25:15.541 --> 00:25:19.333
You're not the man I married.
the one I made a thousand plans with.

392
00:25:19.833 --> 00:25:21.416
If I have to feel alone.

393
00:25:22.041 --> 00:25:23.125
I'd rather be alone.

394
00:25:24.583 --> 00:25:25.833
What do you mean?

395
00:25:27.666 --> 00:25:29.125
I want a divorce.

396
00:25:29.208 --> 00:25:32.416
I won't drink ever again. Maca. okay?

397
00:25:32.500 --> 00:25:36.875
I promise you. please.
but let me show you I can change.

398
00:25:37.458 --> 00:25:39.541
Weren't you going
to a high school reunion?

399
00:25:39.625 --> 00:25:41.291
No. I told Lorena I couldn't go.

400
00:25:41.375 --> 00:25:45.916
No! You need to clear your head. please.
Go. I'll stay with the kids.

401
00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.166
What?
The kids don't take care of themselves!

402
00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:50.416
Maca. please!
If you don't trust me one last time.

403
00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:53.250
how can I show you
what I'm capable of doing for all of you?

404
00:25:55.625 --> 00:25:58.208
Maca. everything will be different
when you come back.

405
00:26:02.958 --> 00:26:04.875
Come on. girl. Relax.

406
00:26:04.958 --> 00:26:07.583
Five calls in three hours. really?

407
00:26:07.666 --> 00:26:11.333
Ricardo put you on the phone with
your in-laws. and they're with the kids.

408
00:26:11.416 --> 00:26:13.708
Yeah. that was reassuring.

409
00:26:13.791 --> 00:26:16.166
Look. you have two options.

410
00:26:16.250 --> 00:26:18.708
You either relax and we have fun.

411
00:26:18.791 --> 00:26:21.583
or you go back to Mexico City.
but not like this. Macaroni.

412
00:26:21.666 --> 00:26:26.791
Right? Yeah. you're right. Okay.
I'll relax. I even feel like dancing.

413
00:26:26.875 --> 00:26:28.208
That's more like it!

414
00:26:52.083 --> 00:26:54.125
Let's go somewhere else.

415
00:26:59.958 --> 00:27:03.750
It was him! Of course it was him!

416
00:27:10.125 --> 00:27:10.958
Maca?

417
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.708
Sorry. we weren't told that…

418
00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.458
Are you okay?

419
00:27:18.250 --> 00:27:20.166
We need to talk about Julieta now.

420
00:27:21.041 --> 00:27:22.291
-Emilio…
-Okay. about what?

421
00:27:25.958 --> 00:27:28.625
I'd ask how you're doing.
but your face says it all.

422
00:27:28.708 --> 00:27:30.541
Come in. please.

423
00:27:30.625 --> 00:27:33.541
I'm so sorry
you can't give your daughter your kidney.

424
00:27:34.166 --> 00:27:38.166
-Like I told Ricardo--
-Yes. I know. but that's not all of it.

425
00:27:43.166 --> 00:27:45.666
Something came up that…

426
00:27:48.833 --> 00:27:51.625
I mean. I didn't see it coming.
I didn't know. I…

427
00:27:57.208 --> 00:27:59.500
Maca. you're scaring us.

428
00:28:00.375 --> 00:28:03.250
Please. you know you can tell us anything.

429
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:05.125
What happened?

430
00:28:14.791 --> 00:28:17.875
Neither Ricardo nor the kids were a match.

431
00:28:18.708 --> 00:28:22.250
That's why we need a private donor.
because if this takes too long.

432
00:28:22.333 --> 00:28:23.708
my daughter could die.

433
00:28:23.791 --> 00:28:24.708
-No.
-No…

434
00:28:24.791 --> 00:28:26.625
-Don't say that.
-That won't happen.

435
00:28:26.708 --> 00:28:27.541
It won't happen.

436
00:28:27.625 --> 00:28:32.458
Please. excuse me. I need to go.
but I'm sure someone will come along.

437
00:28:32.541 --> 00:28:36.083
You know what?
I came here to find that someone.

438
00:28:36.166 --> 00:28:37.625
We've asked…

439
00:28:38.916 --> 00:28:40.666
all our friends for help.

440
00:28:42.166 --> 00:28:47.666
Emilio. could you please
take the test to see if you're a match?

441
00:28:49.208 --> 00:28:51.166
It's important.

442
00:28:53.041 --> 00:28:55.750
Of course. you too. Please.

443
00:28:55.833 --> 00:28:59.291
Listen. Maca. I understand
what you're going through. but…

444
00:29:00.416 --> 00:29:02.458
I'll be completely honest with you.

445
00:29:04.083 --> 00:29:08.458
I'm about to deliver the most important
project of my life. I don't have time--

446
00:29:08.541 --> 00:29:11.458
It takes less than an hour. Emilio.

447
00:29:13.958 --> 00:29:18.000
Look. Maca. unfortunately. we can't
guarantee that we'll take the test.

448
00:29:18.583 --> 00:29:21.458
But why don't you give us
some time to discuss it?

449
00:29:25.625 --> 00:29:26.500
Right…

450
00:29:27.708 --> 00:29:29.333
Sure. I understand.

451
00:29:29.416 --> 00:29:32.750
I trust in our friendship.

452
00:29:34.208 --> 00:29:36.500
Above all. I trust in
our daughters' friendship.

453
00:29:36.583 --> 00:29:40.041
I'll be waiting for you
at the hospital tomorrow. Thank you.

454
00:29:40.125 --> 00:29:41.916
I'll walk you out.

455
00:29:58.208 --> 00:30:01.416
I feel for them.
This can't be easy for Maca and Ricardo.

456
00:30:05.958 --> 00:30:07.708
What's with that look?

457
00:30:07.791 --> 00:30:11.000
Emilio. please. Don't try to fool me.

458
00:30:11.083 --> 00:30:13.708
That woman came to talk to you.

459
00:30:14.291 --> 00:30:17.541
No. That woman
came to ask us to get tested.

460
00:30:17.625 --> 00:30:22.208
No. she came to ask you to get tested.

461
00:30:22.791 --> 00:30:25.416
She was looking at you and talking to you.

462
00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:27.750
I hate it when
you blow things out of proportion.

463
00:30:27.833 --> 00:30:29.875
Maca is still in love with you.
It's obvious.

464
00:30:29.958 --> 00:30:32.083
Please. What are you talking about?

465
00:30:32.666 --> 00:30:37.041
I'm not stupid!
I might look and act stupid. but I'm not!

466
00:30:37.125 --> 00:30:40.375
How can you say she's in love with me
when she ended the relationship?

467
00:30:40.458 --> 00:30:43.375
She dumped me
and didn't want to hear from me again.

468
00:30:43.458 --> 00:30:45.916
and that happened ages ago!

469
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:49.583
And we didn't see each other again
until our daughters met in school.

470
00:30:49.666 --> 00:30:51.208
Do I need to spell it out for you?

471
00:30:52.583 --> 00:30:55.708
-I've got a good nose for these things.
-Maybe COVID fucked it up.

472
00:30:56.291 --> 00:30:59.958
I can't deal with the jealousy.
and your dad is waiting for me.

473
00:31:00.041 --> 00:31:03.791
If we get tested
and one of us happens to be a match.

474
00:31:03.875 --> 00:31:06.791
Ricardo and Maca
will pressure us to be donors.

475
00:31:06.875 --> 00:31:09.250
and to protect my daughters.
I won't allow--

476
00:31:09.333 --> 00:31:11.000
That's enough! Enough!

477
00:31:18.541 --> 00:31:19.833
That's a ten!

478
00:31:19.916 --> 00:31:20.916
Yeah? Is it cool?

479
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:23.333
You just need an accessory
to cover the patch but…

480
00:31:27.916 --> 00:31:29.125
How does it look from above?

481
00:31:29.208 --> 00:31:31.750
You want me to take pictures of you
lying down? Let's see…

482
00:31:31.833 --> 00:31:33.208
Just tell me how it looks.

483
00:31:33.291 --> 00:31:34.833
Weird. but creative.

484
00:31:45.541 --> 00:31:47.708
Hold this for me for a sec. please.

485
00:31:50.208 --> 00:31:52.875
Sorry. Grandma. we've been neglecting you.

486
00:31:53.833 --> 00:31:56.166
Mom's been very busy with me.

487
00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:01.416
Grandma Lucía died before I was born.
She had a heart attack.

488
00:32:02.041 --> 00:32:05.750
Mom says she missed her a lot back then.
but she doesn't remember much anymore.

489
00:32:06.791 --> 00:32:10.375
The longer you've been dead.
the less your loved ones miss you.

490
00:32:12.583 --> 00:32:16.208
When I get a place here. will you visit?
At least for my birthday.

491
00:32:16.291 --> 00:32:21.083
Come on. Give me a break.
You're not going to die. Julieta!

492
00:32:22.375 --> 00:32:23.791
You have one job.

493
00:32:24.875 --> 00:32:27.041
I want to be buried in this dress.

494
00:32:27.625 --> 00:32:30.541
Did you make me come with you
to buy your funeral dress?

495
00:32:30.625 --> 00:32:33.625
If I'd told you. you wouldn't have come.

496
00:32:33.708 --> 00:32:37.666
It'd be embarrassing if everyone saw me
in white and found out I died a virgin.

497
00:32:38.250 --> 00:32:40.583
I'm out. You're crazy! Crazy!

498
00:32:41.333 --> 00:32:43.708
What if I'm cremated instead
to save money?

499
00:32:50.458 --> 00:32:54.375
ESTUDIO DÍAZ
ARCHITECTS

500
00:32:58.583 --> 00:32:59.458
Thank you.

501
00:32:59.541 --> 00:33:03.583
Your brother-in-law is running his mouth.
saying Mr. Díaz will give him the stadium.

502
00:33:04.208 --> 00:33:06.541
Once my father-in-law sees this.
he'll be floored.

503
00:33:06.625 --> 00:33:10.041
I'm the best architect in this firm.
and he knows it.

504
00:33:10.125 --> 00:33:12.666
-Help me cover it.
-This model of yours looks amazing.

505
00:33:12.750 --> 00:33:14.958
But don't get too cocky.

506
00:33:15.041 --> 00:33:16.708
-Okay.
-Family is family.

507
00:33:20.625 --> 00:33:21.791
Good morning. Sergio.

508
00:33:21.875 --> 00:33:24.500
My dad wants to see us both. brother.

509
00:33:24.583 --> 00:33:26.916
Are you his messenger now or what?

510
00:33:32.791 --> 00:33:36.791
The South Africans think
we need their stadium project.

511
00:33:36.875 --> 00:33:41.458
but we have to make them think
that they need us.

512
00:33:41.541 --> 00:33:44.041
You both have to be
at the top of your game.

513
00:33:44.125 --> 00:33:45.583
Don't worry. Dad.

514
00:33:45.666 --> 00:33:49.875
I'm proposing a design
that's very innovative. efficient--

515
00:33:49.958 --> 00:33:52.208
Save the details for the presentation.

516
00:33:52.875 --> 00:33:58.875
If they choose us. one of you is getting
1% of the total construction costs.

517
00:33:58.958 --> 00:34:00.833
That means millions.

518
00:34:00.916 --> 00:34:02.250
May the best man win.

519
00:34:05.458 --> 00:34:08.541
My friend Victoria says that…

520
00:34:09.625 --> 00:34:14.750
I'm not an influencer because I don't post
pictures or videos in my underwear.

521
00:34:16.041 --> 00:34:19.166
Well. today I'm going to show you
my underwear

522
00:34:19.250 --> 00:34:20.500
and something better.

523
00:34:21.041 --> 00:34:22.625
I'm going to make a fool of myself!

524
00:34:22.708 --> 00:34:27.625
But. honestly. I don't care.
because it's just…

525
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.958
It's just the five of you.

526
00:34:38.291 --> 00:34:42.208
Okay. These two tubes right here…

527
00:34:42.291 --> 00:34:44.208
Let me get them out.

528
00:34:44.291 --> 00:34:48.291
Here they are. These tubes you see here…
Can you see them? Okay.

529
00:34:48.375 --> 00:34:51.125
These two tubes right here
are keeping me alive.

530
00:34:51.208 --> 00:34:56.333
And I connect them to this machine.

531
00:34:56.958 --> 00:34:59.041
which filters my blood…

532
00:35:01.833 --> 00:35:03.875
three times a week.

533
00:35:03.958 --> 00:35:07.041
I sit here and wait until it's done.

534
00:35:09.208 --> 00:35:13.333
Well. I've had kidney problems
since I was 15.

535
00:35:13.416 --> 00:35:16.875
and if I don't find a donor soon. well…

536
00:35:17.666 --> 00:35:18.875
I'm royally screwed.

537
00:35:18.958 --> 00:35:21.500
In this case. I'd be renally screwed.

538
00:35:22.791 --> 00:35:24.791
One second. give me a second.

539
00:35:24.875 --> 00:35:29.875
I want to show you what I bought today…

540
00:35:30.625 --> 00:35:34.833
This! Isn't it beautiful?
Wait a second. Let me put it on.

541
00:35:36.250 --> 00:35:37.458
How does it look?

542
00:35:37.958 --> 00:35:41.375
Doesn't it look great?
I love it! I love it! I love it!

543
00:35:41.458 --> 00:35:42.541
Let's see…

544
00:35:43.875 --> 00:35:47.625
I've never had so many people online.

545
00:35:47.708 --> 00:35:48.708
Well…

546
00:35:50.833 --> 00:35:54.250
Thank you. everyone. for saying
positive things. and fuck the haters!

547
00:35:54.333 --> 00:35:57.458
Did you know there are millions of people
with the same problem I have.

548
00:35:57.541 --> 00:35:59.083
so there aren't enough donors?

549
00:35:59.166 --> 00:36:03.541
So it wouldn't hurt if some of you
decided to sign up as donors.

550
00:36:03.625 --> 00:36:08.833
That way. when you kick the bucket.
you could help sick people like me.

551
00:36:08.916 --> 00:36:12.916
Am I going to do another LIVE like this?
Well. I don't know.

552
00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:15.250
Maybe you'll be the last ones
to see me live

553
00:36:15.333 --> 00:36:18.000
because tomorrow I could wake up dead.

554
00:36:18.083 --> 00:36:22.166
Yeah. my kidneys are so messed up
they could take me out at any moment.

555
00:36:23.208 --> 00:36:26.250
Well. I won't say anything else
because TikTok might ban me and…

556
00:36:26.333 --> 00:36:29.708
I'm starting to feel a bit anxious.
so I'm wrapping up the LIVE.

557
00:36:29.791 --> 00:36:32.708
Thanks so much. friends.
and see you next time.

558
00:36:32.791 --> 00:36:34.250
if there is one.

559
00:36:34.333 --> 00:36:35.875
All right. bye.

560
00:37:10.083 --> 00:37:12.833
Maca! I've been looking for you
since I got here!

561
00:37:12.916 --> 00:37:14.791
-Did you see your daughter's LIVE?
-No.

562
00:37:14.875 --> 00:37:16.333
Brace yourself.

563
00:37:18.166 --> 00:37:20.416
…I've had kidney problems since I was 15.

564
00:37:20.500 --> 00:37:23.750
and if I don't find a donor soon.
I'm royally screwed.

565
00:37:24.583 --> 00:37:25.833
They'll be online any minute.

566
00:37:25.916 --> 00:37:28.416
According to the schedule.
you start. Emilio.

567
00:37:28.500 --> 00:37:29.958
-Yes. sir.
-It's night over there.

568
00:37:30.041 --> 00:37:34.291
I need everyone
to be full of energy. okay?

569
00:37:34.375 --> 00:37:35.958
I'm ready. Carlos.

570
00:37:36.541 --> 00:37:38.583
-I'm ready too. Dad--
-Yeah. yeah.

571
00:37:49.208 --> 00:37:50.666
What is it. Pedro?

572
00:37:52.833 --> 00:37:56.208
Sorry. Carlos. I need to make
some adjustments to the presentation.

573
00:37:56.791 --> 00:38:00.000
-I won't be long. One minute. please.
-Seriously. man?

574
00:38:13.708 --> 00:38:15.250
You can't just show up like this!

575
00:38:15.333 --> 00:38:19.833
What makes you think you can
threaten Pedro so I come talk to you?

576
00:38:19.916 --> 00:38:22.208
I'm in the most important meeting
of my life--

577
00:38:22.291 --> 00:38:23.875
Julieta is your daughter.

578
00:38:23.958 --> 00:38:26.375
and she needs you to donate your kidney!

579
00:38:32.333 --> 00:38:35.666
1 IN EVERY 25 FATHERS

580
00:38:35.750 --> 00:38:38.166
IS RAISING ANOTHER'S MAN CHILD.

581
00:38:38.250 --> 00:38:42.083
AND IN MOST CASES.

582
00:38:42.166 --> 00:38:49.166
THEY NEVER FIND OUT.

583
00:42:06.666 --> 00:42:09.583
Subtitle translation by: Alicia Núñez
